cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DUET, please cite the manuscript below (preferred-citation) and the software."
type: software
title: "DUET"
abstract: >-
  DUET (Decoding Unified with Experimental Trade-offs) designs codebooks for
  barcode-based assays such as optical pooled screens and MERFISH by trading
  decoding accuracy against an experiment-specific objective, and returns the
  Pareto front of codebooks.
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AltschulerWu-Lab/DUET"
keywords:
  - codebook design
  - barcodes
  - error correction
  - multi-objective optimization
  - optical pooled screens
  - MERFISH
authors:
